Parity notes: this surface is the SwiftUI counterpart of the gold-standard sibling
SentryEventLogWidget (same "event log" tier). It merges TWO web data sources —
useAuditLogs (/system/audit) + useSecurityEvents (/security?vehicle_id=) — into one
newest-first feed, exactly as the web AuditLogWidget does. The web `inferAuditSeverity`,
`inferSecuritySeverity`, `buildSecurityTitle`, the `feedItems` map ([...logs,...events]),
the `isCompact = size.cols <= 1` big-number variant (WidgetBigNumber), `maxItems={15}`,
and the `totalEvents24h`/`worstSeverity` 24h memo are all ported and unit-tested. Every
hardcoded English literal in the web `buildSecurityTitle` is routed through the P1/S10
facade (no literals in Swift). Shared P4-core types (DashboardWidgetSize/Registration)
and P1/S9 tokens (Color.TS/Font.TS/TSSpacing/TSRadius/TSTone/TSSkeleton) are consumed,
NOT redefined — matching SentryEventLogWidget (this surface adds no duplicate core type).

