========================================================================
The prompt gate runs `xcodebuild -scheme TeslaSync ... build test` and
`xcodebuild -scheme TeslaSync-macOS build test`. These compile the WHOLE app target,
whose sources include the entire TeslaSync/dashboard-widgets + TeslaSync/feature-views
trees (project.yml). In the current aggregate repo that target does NOT compile, for
reasons entirely OUTSIDE this surface's allowed-files scope (AuditLogWidget.* only):

  • 13 sibling files each define `public struct DashboardWidgetSize` AND
    `public struct DashboardWidgetRegistration` at top level in the same module
    => guaranteed "invalid redeclaration" once the module is built together.
    (verify: grep -rlE "public struct DashboardWidgetSize" \
       apps/apple/TeslaSync/dashboard-widgets apps/apple/TeslaSync/feature-views | wc -l  => 13)
  • 260 files under those app-target source dirs carry `@testable import TeslaSync`
    + `import XCTest` (the per-surface *.Tests.swift convention). XCTest is not
    linked into the app target => guaranteed failure.
    (verify: grep -rlE "@testable import TeslaSync" \
       apps/apple/TeslaSync/dashboard-widgets apps/apple/TeslaSync/feature-views | wc -l  => 260)
  • The TeslaSync scheme build preAction stages the KMP `Shared.xcframework`
    (Scripts/build-shared-xcframework.sh — Gradle/JDK/Kotlin-Native), absent here.

These are known properties of the parallel per-surface generation methodology; the
shared P4-core types are de-duplicated and the *.Tests.swift files are relocated into
the XCTest targets during a later integration/reconciliation phase that is NOT in this
surface's allowed-files list. This surface deliberately conforms to the convention
(it adds NO 14th duplicate of the core types and mirrors the sibling test placement),
so it integrates cleanly once that reconciliation runs.

